{"name":"Smokescreen","hex":"#5e5755","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"smokescreen","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Smoke used as a disguise, mask or cover, as of troops in battle.","Anything used metaphorically to conceal or distract."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/smokescreen"}],"entries":[{"title":"Security smoke","blocks":[{"text":"Security smoke is a thermally generated white fog, aimed at inhibiting intruders from accessing items to steal, much used in the storage of high-value goods, and recommended by police and insurers. It consists of glycol or glycerine mixed with distilled water, which vaporises and then condenses in the air."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7d/2%D1%8F_%D1%81%D0%B5%D0%BA%D1%83%D0%BD%D0%B4%D0%B0_%D0%BF%D0%BE%D1%81%D0%BB%D0%B5_%D0%B0%D0%BA%D1%82%D0%B8%D0%B2%D0%B0%D1%86%D0%B8%D0%B8_Smoke_Screen.jpg/330px-2%D1%8F_%D1%81%D0%B5%D0%BA%D1%83%D0%BD%D0%B4%D0%B0_%D0%BF%D0%BE%D1%81%D0%BB%D0%B5_%D0%B0%D0%BA%D1%82%D0%B8%D0%B2%D0%B0%D1%86%D0%B8%D0%B8_Smoke_Screen.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Security_smoke","wikidata":"Q7445068"},{"title":"Smokescreen (film)","blocks":[{"text":"Smokescreen is a 1964 British comedy crime drama film, written and directed by Jim O'Connolly and starring Peter Vaughan."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/e/ec/%22Smokescreen%22_%281964%29.jpg/330px-%22Smokescreen%22_%281964%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Smokescreen_(film)","wikidata":"Q7545945"},{"title":"Smoke screen","blocks":[{"text":"A smoke screen is smoke released to mask the movement or location of military units such as infantry, tanks, aircraft, or ships."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f8/Massachusetts_National_Guard_%2827773978964%29.jpg/330px-Massachusetts_N